meta {
  name: Research
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/knowledge/research
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "question": "Why doesn't selfmemory use a vector database any more, and who decided?",
    "timeout": 240
  }
}

tests {
  test("answers, or says the runtime is unavailable", function () {
    expect([200, 503]).to.include(res.getStatus());
  });

  test("citations name pages that exist", function () {
    if (res.getStatus() !== 200) return;
    expect(res.getBody().citations).to.be.an("array");
    expect(res.getBody().projects).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

settings {
  timeout: 300000
}

docs {
  The deep read path. Materializes the project's pages into a disposable
  directory, runs an agent over them with read-only tools, then wipes it.

  **Expect this to take 10-60 seconds.** The Bruno timeout above is raised to
  5 minutes to match; the server caps `timeout` at 600s.

  Answers multi-hop questions the fast path cannot: following `[[links]]`,
  reconciling two pages, tracing when a decision changed. Citations are
  validated against real slugs, so a page the model invents is dropped rather
  than returned.

  ### Querying several projects

  Send `project_ids` instead of `project_id`:

      { "question": "...", "project_ids": ["<id-a>", "<id-b>"] }

  Every id is authorized individually and an unauthorized one is rejected —
  the request fails rather than quietly returning a narrower answer. Projects
  marked isolated are never included. A project API key is pinned to one
  project, so cross-project research needs session auth.

  ### Failure modes

  - `503` — the `opencode` binary is not on the server's PATH. `Ask` still works.
  - `502` — the agent session failed or exceeded `timeout`.
}
